WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.800
I wanted to add a little personal note to the top of show.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.950
I'm someone who puts a tremendous amount

3
00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:09.080
of pressure on myself, and that is putting it so politely.

4
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:09.980
And like (growls).

5
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.110
And I live in that pressure cooker state.

6
00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.100
And the other day, for some unknown to me reason,

7
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.570
I thought, can you think about the things that you've done,

8
00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:24.630
rather than you need to do.

9
00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:29.630
And I took some inventory, and so I thought as an exercise

10
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:33.380
as we make all of our to-do lists,

11
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:38.380
try to maybe make a have-done list as well.

12
00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.920
And I see people nodding their heads in the wall

13
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.240
and I can't tell you what a sense of community

14
00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:46.700
I feel right now, so thank you for this moment.

15
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:47.880
It means a lot to me.

16
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.523
And of course, as soon as I had it I thought,

17
00:00:49.523 --> 00:00:51.720
well, what do I do with it?

18
00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.960
Let's share it, all right.
(audience clapping)

19
00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:57.980
Now, ironically, I would like to introduce you to someone

20
00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:02.560
who already has a have-done list at her age

21
00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.560
that is so incredibly impressive, it blows my mind, okay?

22
00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:12.580
Imagine setting out to feed the hungry, shelter the homeless

23
00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.000
and help those who are less fortunate

24
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.360
at just seven years old.

25
00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:24.360
And now, at age 14, double the number, Sanya Pirani

26
00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:28.977
from Minneapolis, Minnesota has created the organization

27
00:01:28.977 --> 00:01:32.660
"Sanya's Hope For Children" in order to help young people

28
00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:36.160
get the supplies they need, to succeed.

29
00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:40.270
So, without further ado, and everything aside,

30
00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.754
can we please welcome Sonya!

31
00:01:42.754 --> 00:01:45.600
(audience clapping)

32
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.640
Hello, and may I ask, will you explain

33
00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.940
what "Sanya's Hope For Children" is?

34
00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:55.460 line:15%
Well, "Sanya's Hope For Children" is a 501(c)(3)

35
00:01:55.460 --> 00:02:00.100 line:15%
student-lead, non-profit founded in 2017, January

36
00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:04.600
and we're focused on children helping children

37
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.330
and our mission is that we strongly believe

38
00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:09.530
that every child deserves basic human rights.

39
00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:14.020
Like food, shelter, clothes, safety and education.

40
00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:16.860
You are just incredible.

41
00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.560
Will you please tell us about the latest project

42
00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.020
that you are working on, I believe it's

43
00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:24.433
collecting toys for homeless children.

44
00:02:25.451 --> 00:02:26.960
Yeah, so this project is called

45
00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:31.740
our "Christmas Bag Project" and we take volunteers,

46
00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:35.200
my own Santa's Helper children team and myself,

47
00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.140
we all sew these bags, and then we have donations

48
00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:40.490
of school supplies, toys and books,

49
00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:43.680
which are then put into the bags during an event

50
00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.430
and then for this year, they will be delivered

51
00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.730
to homeless shelters around Minnesota.

52
00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.400
Well, we'd like to help.

53
00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:54.840
We're gonna donate $10,000 to "Sanya's Hope For Children"

54
00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:58.253
to help you continue the amazing work that you do.

55
00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:00.770
Oh my God, that's so amazing!

56
00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:03.880
I really appreciate it, thank you so much.

57
00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:05.067
That is, oh my God.

58
00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:09.360
Thank you for setting an example for us all

59
00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:12.801
and we're gonna have your organization up on our website.

60
00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:14.640
You're just incredible;

61
00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.200
I'm so honored that you came on the show.

62
00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.790 line:15%
Well, I am so glad to have this opportunity

63
00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:23.140 line:15%
to come on the show, meeting with you has been so amazing.

64
00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:26.510 line:15%
I am so appreciative of you, thank you so much.

65
00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:29.300
Well, right back at you, thank you Sanya, thank you.

66
00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.709 line:15%
We'll see you soon and check back in with you.

67
00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:34.292 line:15%
(upbeat music)

